1:1 leading ImportDecl 2:1 "# A def may follow an import with no empty line, so one written with a body gets none there either."
4:1 leading ExportDecl 10:1 "# A one-line def stays one when it fits. A one-line def too long for its line (an exported one with a `##` doc too),"
5:1 leading ExportDecl 10:1 "# or whose value takes lines of its own (a pipe chain of two or more `|>`), is written as the def with a body that it"
6:1 leading ExportDecl 10:1 "# stands for: the value is its last line, with no `return`. A trailing comment stays on the line, and a value spread"
7:1 leading ExportDecl 10:1 "# over lines inside parentheses or with a leading `.` is joined when it fits."
12:1 leading ExportDecl 17:1 "# One-line defs may follow each other with no empty line, and `fmt` keeps the author's choice. One that is too long"
13:1 leading ExportDecl 17:1 "# for its line is written with a body, and gets the empty lines of a declaration on both sides, so the output still"
14:1 leading ExportDecl 17:1 "# parses; its neighbours stay one line."
19:1 leading ExportDecl 28:1 "# A def whose body is one `return value` is written as a one-line def when that fits on its line: with a `##` doc and"
20:1 leading ExportDecl 28:1 "# `export` too, with comment lines right before it and right after its `end`, and when the source spreads the value"
21:1 leading ExportDecl 28:1 "# over lines that the layout joins (arguments, a `.name` line, a `do` block that fits), and for `try`. It keeps its"
22:1 leading ExportDecl 28:1 "# body when a comment sits from its `def` line to its `end` line, when the value takes lines of its own (a pipe chain"
23:1 leading ExportDecl 28:1 "# of two or more `|>`, a `case`), when it does not fit, when the body is anything else (two statements, a guard, a bare"
24:1 leading ExportDecl 28:1 "# `return`), and for a Void function (`main` included). The empty lines are kept as found. A body that stays gives"
25:1 leading ExportDecl 28:1 "# its value without `return` (#1287), but for a `case` value and in a Void function."
36:35 trailing FunctionDecl 36:1 "# twice"
51:1 leading FunctionDecl 52:1 "# a note"
62:1 leading FunctionDecl 63:1 "# a note before"
66:1 leading FunctionDecl 68:1 "# a note after"
68:26 trailing TypeRef 68:22 "# on the def line"
73:3 leading Return 74:3 "# inside"
79:5 trailing FunctionDecl 77:1 "# on the end line"
137:1 leading FunctionDecl 139:1 "# A one-line def whose value is a `try` and that does not fit is written with `return`: a `try` at the end of a body"
138:1 leading FunctionDecl 139:1 "# is a statement, so the bare value would not give it."
